      trivia: "【Vitola Names as an Anthropology Lecture】The CroMagnon vitolas — Anthropology, Cranium, Mandible, Femur, EMH (Early Modern Human, that is, anatomically modern humans) and Knuckle Dragger — are named almost entirely from the vocabulary of palaeoanthropology. Peștera Muierilor is the name of a real cave in Romania where the bones of Palaeolithic humans were unearthed.【Half the Factory Belongs to a Nicaraguan】While the brand company RoMa Craft Tobac is a joint venture of Rosales and Martin, the Nica Sueño factory is owned fifty-fifty by Martin and Esteban Disla, who serves as factory manager. Few American-owned boutiques have a local artisan holding half the factory.【A Craft Beer Bar at Headquarters】The new headquarters opened in Austin, Texas in February 2016 measures about 4,000 square feet and holds, besides the warehouse and packing workshop, a lounge, a display humidor and a craft beer bar — a statement that the “Craft” in the name is more than a turn of phrase.【A Prohibition Brand with a Vitola Named for Drink】With the addition of Whiskey Rebellion 1794, on the revolt against the whiskey tax (1791–94), to the temperance-themed Intemperance, the company's range came to embrace both the side that bans drink and the side that rises up for it.【Maestranza Named from a Television Programme】The name of the US-exclusive line is said to derive from words spoken by the Argentine chef Francis Mallmann in the television series “Chef's Table” about the people who help at one's side."
