      trivia: "【Two Jobs at Once】In the early days Nick Jr is said to have kept his 75,000-dollar post as an air traffic controller, living a double life — the control tower by day, rolling cigars with his wife Janine in the garage by night. The discipline and precision instilled by the Navy are credited with shaping the rigorous quality control of later years.\n【The Secret of the “Champagne”】The process of giving wrapper leaf additional ageing in bourbon barrels was named “Champagne” by Nick Sr, and its details remain a family secret. The idea of resting long-aged leaf further in barrels became the single greatest hallmark dividing the company's premium lines from those of other houses."
